# Architecture

Keep a strict separation of concerns:

```text
Frontend UI → frontend services → REST API → controllers → services → Prisma → PostgreSQL
```

- Do not put business logic or database access in React components.
- Keep Express route handlers thin. Validation, auth, and persistence belong in dedicated modules.
- Authentication is centralized in `backend/src/auth` and `backend/src/services/auth.service.ts`.
- Shared validation and public types live in `shared/` and must stay in sync for client and server.
- New pages should reuse `AppShell` and `ProtectedRoute`. New APIs should follow `/api/<domain>` with a controller/service pair.
- WhatsApp Cloud API is a channel into `sendChatMessage` (`/api/whatsapp/webhook`). Do not add a second LLM path for inbound WhatsApp.
- Lucy and every other digital employee emit the same base action catalog (`lists`, `filing`, `messages`, `directory`, `reminders`, `query`, `confirm`, `handoff`) from `LLM.config.json` / `LLM.action.json`. New digital workers inherit that Lucy base; future capability add-ons can layer on top. Handoff is only a conversation switch. The worker asks until the schema is complete, then emits it. The server only applies those fields and fires them. A self-nudge is several actions: speaker shopping or task, a task on the digital worker they spoke to, and a reminder clock. `EmployeeListItems.reminder_id` and `Reminders.worker_item_id` are a two-way link between that worker task and the clock (`ON DELETE CASCADE` both ways). Deleting the clock deletes the worker task; deleting the worker task deletes the clock. The speaker item is not cascade-linked via FK; on cancel the model may also `lists.remove` that speaker wrapper when it matches the cancelled nudge (or ask if it looks like independent work). On `lists.remove` of a shopping/task item the server also cancels active clocks that match the same work by key/label. Custom lists always need a real `EmployeeLists.name` (from speech / item `list_name`; ask only if missing) — never leave `name=""`. After a one-shot clock fires, the reminder is marked `status=done` with `sent_at` / `send_status` (not deleted) and kept in the DB for 14 days; the worker task is detached and soft-deleted (`deleted_at`) so Lucy does not keep an open job. `sent_text` is `last_composed_text` or the fixed `message_text`. Every-turn `EMPLOYEE_SAVED_DATA` includes active reminders only; done/cancelled clock history loads when the model emits `query: "report"` with `sections` including `reminders` and/or `sends` (or full report). Ask whether a self-reminder already fired / מתי נשלחה → `sections:["reminders"]`; ask what we already sent to someone else → `sections:["sends"]`; ask what was deleted/cancelled / מתי ביטלנו → `sections:["history"]` (server formats recent `AuditEvents` removes/updates, 14 days). Scope history with a companion domain (`history`+`shopping` = shopping only) and/or `history_kinds` (`add`|`update`|`remove`|`fire`). List items and filings soft-delete via `deleted_at` (partial unique so the same key can be re-added); reminder cancel sets `status=cancelled`. Mutations append to `AuditEvents`. `Contacts` is the speaker's personal phone book (`metadata.directory`); resolve message/reminder targets via Employees first, then SPEAKER_CONTACTS. Do not create Employees for outsiders (Contacts is the phone book). WhatsApp inbound may still create a temporary `אורח` employee shell for the session; hide those guests from the Employees UI and Chat-as picker. `Employees.is_owner` marks account owners (any number of humans, including zero). Non-owners only receive their own EMPLOYEE_SAVED_DATA; an owner receives every human's lists/tasks/filings/clocks. Personal contacts stay speaker-only. Reminder delete confirmation is server Action State on the conversation (`pending_action` / `pending_targets` / `pending_step`), injected each turn — not LLM memory. The same Action State holds incomplete multi-turn drafts (`hold`: directory/lists/reminders/filing + `need`) so a short follow-up (last name, time, phone) completes the draft instead of «לא הבנתי». Phone-book adds (אנשי קשר + name + digits) use `metadata.directory` (first name is enough — last name is optional on lists.contacts). Filings (`תיוקים`) are durable speaker facts/memory; the model decides what to file, and every turn the server injects all visible filings in `EMPLOYEE_SAVED_DATA` (no separate retrieval query for POC). Scheduled outbound may set `compose: true` so `message_text` is a brief and the final WhatsApp copy is written by the LLM at fire time (generic; not birthday-specific). After each compose fire, `last_composed_text` stores the last send so the next run can avoid repeating it. Optional `compose_source` selects a fire-time data source for the brief (today: `git_log` reads repo commits since `last_report_sha` and summarizes in English — platform-owner recipe, not a global capability catalog item; future sources can plug in the same way). Reminder update/match searches all active clocks for the user (any owner), then keeps `owner_id` from the existing row. List remove/update resolves `list_type` from where the item actually lives (shopping vs tasks); if the spoken reply says קניות for a tasks remove, the server corrects it to מטלות. `query: "todos"` / `"self"` / `"reminders"` tell the model which saved data to read. `query: "report"` asks for a status report; optional `sections` (`reminders` | `sends` | `tasks` | `shopping` | `filings` | `contacts` | `custom` | `history`) request a partial report — the server formats the Hebrew report from saved data (`reminders`/`sends` include recent done/cancelled; `history` is audit deletes/updates). The model writes `response` for normal answers (product Hebrew only — never schema jargon like `list_name` / `metadata`). The server does not invent that answer, but may correct known false delivery claims, wrong shopping/tasks list wording after apply, and may replace the spoken reply for `query: "report"`. Exact relative day labels (`היום` / `מחר` / `אתמול`) in list item fields are normalized to `YYYY-MM-DD` (Asia/Jerusalem) on save and in report formatting — this is not weekday/intent parsing. Do not parse user intent with regex, and do not add engine shortcuts (`item: "all"`, inventing clocks from weekday words in free text, harvesting phones from item text).
- Do not implement registration, password reset, social login, or roles unless explicitly requested.
